# Wave W17-U (Ruined Path): old road floor — broken paving flags: the old road’s own slabs, grey stone flags laid in cracked joints, carrying pale niche-glint flecks where the wall niches catch what light the hill lets in (design: the path was a road before it was a cave, and remembers both; the shipped drip water, rock and caveboulder stand byte-preserved beside it). The Ruined Path’s own floor — split from Copperbore Tunnel’s tidy tool-brown bore flags (Maris) by temperature and condition: this floor is grey, cracked, and fallen-in, that one brown, dressed, and swept.
